# Do not code on `main`

`main` is merge-only. Do not edit files, commit, or land features while `HEAD` is `main`.

Before any implementation:

1. Check `git branch --show-current`.
2. If it is `main`, create or check out a topic branch (`feat/…`, `fix/…`, `chore/…`) first.
3. Keep `main` in sync with the remote via merge/PR only. Do not reset or force-push `main` unless the user explicitly asks.
